# Staged by fisher-4yn.1 on 2026-11-25 for a search that makes cutoffs.
# Successor of uci/go-depth.uci (fisher-5sg.5, 2026-11-25), whose sources stand:
# April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/,
# fisher-8ie, fisher-r6y D20, D24, D28 and D41, fisher-5sg decisions 2–6 and 10.
# Perft: expectations/perft.epd. Full info spelling: Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d),
# as cited in expectations/README.md. See README.md beside this session.
#
# Every node total at depth 2 or more reads {nodes}, as in uci/. One limit
# changes: the node limit beside depth 1 was 440, the total at which depth 2
# finishes without cutoffs. With cutoffs depth 2 finishes at 79 (the
# derivation is in go-nodes.uci beside this session), so 440 becomes 79 and
# the node limit again sits exactly where depth 2 would finish.
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# Depth 0 reaches the limit before any node is entered (D20).
> go depth 0
< bestmove h8g8

# An explicit limit can exceed the default depth of 4 (D28).
> go depth 5
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< info depth 5 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< bestmove h8g8

# The finished depth is reported before stop releases the held move.
> go infinite depth 1
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8
> isready
< readyok
> stop
< bestmove h8g8

> position startpos
> go depth 1
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}
> go depth 2
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

# Depth reaches its limit first with either parameter order. 79 nodes
# would let depth 2 finish (fisher-4yn: 440 becomes 79).
> go depth 1 nodes 79
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}
> go nodes 79 depth 1
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

# Nodes reach their limit first with either parameter order.
> go depth 2 nodes 20
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}
> go nodes 20 depth 2
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

# Terminal root (fisher-2aj.2 owner approval, 2026-11-23).
> position fen 7k/6Q1/5K2/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go depth 2
< info depth 0 score mate 0
< bestmove 0000

# The terminal response precedes the zero limit.
> go depth 0
< info depth 0 score mate 0
< bestmove 0000

> quit
! exit
